This is part of the <frameset> tag, which replaces the <body> tag when using frames in older HTML.

rows="30%,70%" means:

The browser window is divided horizontally into two parts (rows):

The first row takes up 30% of the window height.

The second row takes up 70% of the window height.
----------------------------  ← 30% (top frame - top.html)
|                          |
|      Top Frame           |
|                          |
----------------------------  ← 70% (split into two columns)

|        |                |
|  Left  |    Right       |
| Frame  |    Frame       |
|        |                |
----------------------------


This tag splits the area vertically into two columns.

cols="50%,50%" means:

+--------------------------+
|                          | ← Top frame (30%)
+-----------+--------------+
|           |              |
| Left      |   Right      | ← Bottom frame split into 2 columns (each 50%)
| Frame     |   Frame      |
|           |              |
+-----------+--------------+



